{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386886-mage-population","id":1386886,"title":"Mage Population","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T20:12:53-07:00","id":1386886,"title":"Mage Population","content":"Does anyone remember the original mention of how many mages per person in the WOD there were?<br /> <br /> More importantly, was there anything like that in M20 (I don't recall any)?<br /> <br /> And finally, in games you've run or played, what were those numbers more like? A chantry of each tradition in a major city? A handful of mages in a nation? 50 in a small town? That sort of thing if you don't have solid numbers. <br /> <br /> Just curious, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:29:56-07:00","id":1386892,"title":"","content":"Check out Ascension's Landscape, in Storyteller's Vault. It doesn't give authoritative figures, but it does address the question quite thoroughly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T21:33:39-07:00","id":1386902,"title":"","content":"I try to play it as a percentage game (Ascensions Landscape does a great job exploring this). One in a million would equal to about 7000 magi in the world. I do not imagine it would be an even distribution. The Awakened may tend to migrate and congregate to/in certain areas.<br /> To help me grasp what this ratio pans out to be, I compare it to the rate of other conditions. So, out of a million people, I would figure...<br /> 1 Mage<br /> 100 people with Situs inversus (mirrored organs, with the heart on the right and so forth) one in ten thousand<br /> 17000 Intersexed chromosomes (xxy or xyy), about one in sixty<br /> 60000 Birth defects of various sorts, about one in seventeen<br /> <br /> I tried to find the rates of myostatin deficient hypertrophy, but that is so rare that there is no known statistical data. The reason I wanted to include that number is because it is a real llegit super power. Natural low body fat and Hercules build &amp; strength, without ever having to work out ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:02:20-07:00","id":1386907,"title":"","content":"While not official, Paul Strack's work on Mage Demographics back when Ander's Mage Page was a major Mage fan site, is pretty good. Ander's Mage Page has been partially reconstructed, and includes Strack's article. Ascension's Landscape is working on a similar premise, but has a lot more detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://mage.gearsonline.net/anders/misc/storytelling/demography2.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://mage.gearsonline.net/anders/img/title01.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mage.gearsonline.net/anders/misc/storytelling/demography2.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Demographics in Mage 2 - Anders Mage Page 2.0 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://mage.gearsonline.net/anders/misc/storytelling/demography2.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://mage.gearsonline.net/anders/misc/storytelling/demography2.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I use percentage of world population and much like other posters, consider there to be clusters of mages. The size of a chantry in my stories and in games I've played in is usually the PCs+a few NPCs since I like to play from disciples up (and we never got to Master level in a Sphere). I have only played or run Tradition games and usually made the Technocracy about twice as big in the area.<br /> <br /> I've usually had 3 or 4 regular players. Right now I have 5 players but one is fairly inactive, so the Tradition chantry is basically 4 PCs and 4 NPCs. Though the chantry is likely to add a few NPCs soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T04:35:01-07:00","id":1386947,"title":"","content":"These are the numbers that Malcolm Sheppard (Revised edition Lead writer) gave once.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Canonically, the largest are:</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) OoH (they recruit more than any other Trad and the House structure lets them incorporate many different styles)</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Akashic Brotherhood (they recruit less than many Trads but have the largest population base to draw from).</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">After that, the Dreamspeakers and Celestial Chorus are supposed to be pretty large and diverse. The Verbena trail slightly behind these two. The Ecstatics are probably about the size of the Verbena.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether are probably about equal size and next largest after the trads above.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Euthanatos are supposed to be smaller than the other Traditions.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">To make some hard choices and put it all in a list, with breakdowns the ranking from largest to smallest would be:</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) Order of Hermes 15%</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Akashic Brotherhood 14%</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3) Celestial Chorus 13%</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4) Dreamspeakers 12%</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5) Verbena 11%*</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6) Cult of Ecstacy 11%*</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">7) Virtual Adepts 9%*</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">8) Sons of Ether 9%*</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">9) Euthanatos 6%</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">*The higher ranks Trad may have a fractionally higher number of members.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Bill Bridges revised the numbers during his run, which were originally 1 mage per million or 1 per 500,000, to 1 per 200,000 ro 250,000. Let's make it an even 30,000 Awakened mages in the world.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">That means the Traditions have 12,000 members.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">So:</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1) Order of Hermes: 1800</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2) Akashic Brotherhood: 1680</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3) Celestial Chorus: 1560</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4) Dreamspeakers: 1440</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5) Verbena: 1320</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6) Cult of Ecstacy: 1320</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">7) Virtual Adepts: 1080</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">8) Sons of Ether: 1080</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">9) Euthanatos: 720</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Breakdown by rank makes most Tradition mages Disciples, with a significant narrowing at Adept rank thanks to attrition and fewer apprentices because they tend to die more easily and because magic is generally in decline. So:</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Apprentice 15% -- 1800 Traditionalists</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Initiate: 20% -- 2400 Traditionalists</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Disciple: 50% -- 6000 Traditionalists</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Adept: 13% -- 1560 Traditionalists</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Master: 1.9% -- 228 Traditionalists?</span></i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Archmaster: .1% 12 Traditionalists?</span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ranks will tend to break statistical predictions as the increase. For instance, thr Masters and archmasters are probably doled out more evenly that Tradition numbers would suggest. By contrast, the Technocracy probably has a fairly strict pyramidial distribution, with the fewest </span></i></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">on top and as many as half being &quot;Apprentices.&quot;</span></i></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:49:08-07:00","id":1386999,"title":"","content":"Cool. I was curious, because I wanted some guidelines for when I write an Adventure for other Storyteller's to use I didn't want to go too far from general expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}